# Every production arm that passes over a refusal unread (`Err(_) =>
# continue | break | {}`), counted per file (scripts/gates/escalation-discards.sh).
# A search over readings that keeps nothing refuses, where none decides,
# with a cause that is not the reading that stopped it: that is
# `geom_brep::ladder::climb`'s job, which keeps and ranks what it passes
# over. A new discard reds until it is registered here with why it is not
# a search's kept reading; a count that falls reds until it is lowered.
#
# half_angle: the noise meter's reading in the gap runs the ladder, which
# then reads (and keeps) its own margins; no search passes over it.
crates/geom-brep/src/half_angle.rs 1
# ssi/boundary: an in-band corner distance falls through to the corner's
# class, the next reading of the same corner; a poisoned one refuses.
crates/geom-brep/src/ssi/boundary.rs 1
# profile seg: a poisoned straightness reading falls through to the
# carrier's checks after it, which read the same segment.
crates/profile/src/seg.rs 1
# join seam_germ_side: a region normal refused in band is dropped from the
# chord read; filed as a hand-rolled search with its agreement check
# (work/onecopy/door-searches-left-on-the-hand-rolled-ladder.md).
crates/topo/src/boolean/join.rs 1
# census: the detector's posture: a pair whose interiors do not decide is
# neither overlap nor apart, and the census reports what decided.
crates/topo/src/census.rs 1
# offset_derive: a net with no interior iso column is no planar-offset
# candidate; a structural refusal, not an escalation.
crates/topo/src/offset_derive.rs 1
# validate check 3's flux arm: argued in place; check 7 reports the cause.
crates/topo/src/validate.rs 1
